  "slug": "code-architecture-review",
  "name": "Code Architecture Review",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Drop this plugin into any project and ask Claude to \"review my architecture.\" It scans for clean architecture violations, SOLID breaches, code smells, and structural anti-patterns across Node.js, Python, React, Go, and monorepo setups — then hands you a prioritized report with actionable fixes, not just vague warnings.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, `code-architecture-review` (Use this skill whenever the user wants to audit, review, or improve the architecture of a codebase).\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install code-architecture-review@claude-community` from `Farjmand/code-architecture-review`.\n\nA Claude Code plugin that audits your codebase for architectural issues, code smells, SOLID violations, and file structure problems — then hands you a prioritized, actionable report.",
